<h2>Which filter layout for Account activity?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">All three cover failed sign-ins, security changes, and one week. They differ in how many controls there are and how precise the week choice is. Wireframes only; real styling will use the guideline tokens.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">A: Two selects</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end">
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;font-size:14px">Show
              <select class="mock-input"><option>All events</option><option>Failed sign-ins</option><option>Security changes</option><option disabled>──────</option><option>Sign-in</option><option>Sign-out</option><option>…all nine types</option></select>
            </label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;font-size:14px">Week
              <select class="mock-input"><option>All 90 days</option><option>Sep 28 – Oct 4, 2026</option><option>Sep 21 – 27, 2026</option><option>…13 weeks</option></select>
            </label>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:13px;margin:12px 0 4px">Showing 8 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A: Two selects</h3>
      <p>"Show" has the two shortcuts first, then each of the nine types. "Week" lists the last 13 weeks. Most compact, smallest diff.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">B: Radio views + week select</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <fieldset style="border:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 12px">
            <legend style="font-size:14px;margin-bottom:6px">Show</legend>
            <label><input type="radio" name="b" checked> All events</label>&nbsp;&nbsp;
            <label><input type="radio" name="b"> Failed sign-ins</label>&nbsp;&nbsp;
            <label><input type="radio" name="b"> Security changes</label>
          </fieldset>
          <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;font-size:14px;width:max-content">Week
            <select class="mock-input"><option>All 90 days</option><option>Sep 28 – Oct 4, 2026</option><option>…13 weeks</option></select>
          </label>
          <p style="font-size:13px;margin:12px 0 4px">Showing 8 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B: Radio views + week select</h3>
      <p>The two shortcuts are visible with one click, no menu to open. You can't pick a single other type (e.g. only Sign-out).</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">C: Select + date range</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end">
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;font-size:14px">Show
              <select class="mock-input"><option>All events</option><option>Failed sign-ins</option><option>Security changes</option></select>
            </label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;font-size:14px">Start date
              <input class="mock-input" type="date" value="2026-09-21">
            </label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;font-size:14px">End date
              <input class="mock-input" type="date" value="2026-09-27">
            </label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;font-size:14px">Preset
              <select class="mock-input"><option>Last 7 days</option><option>Last 30 days</option><option>Custom</option></select>
            </label>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:13px;margin:12px 0 4px">Showing 8 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>C: Select + date range</h3>
      <p>Any span of days, not just calendar weeks. Four controls, adds end-before-start validation; roughly 80–100 more lines than A.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
